def add(i,title,plain,claim,model,paths,novelty,limits,significance,rank=None,status='accepted',category='restricted theorem',sources=(),related=(),inspection='Theorem and/or accepted audit read as inert text in this pass; no supplied program executed, imported, compiled or AST-parsed.'):
 ev=[]
 for p in paths:
  f=ROOT/p
  if not f.exists(): raise FileNotFoundError(p)
  ev.append({'archive_relative_path':p,'workspace_path':str(f),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(f.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'inspection':inspection})
 rows.append({'stable_id':i,'title':title,'plain_meaning':plain,'exact_claim':claim,'model':model,'proof_status':status,'evidence_level':'Internally independently audited within stated scope; not external peer review or priority certification' if status=='accepted' else status,'category':category,'evidence':ev,'novelty_delta':novelty,'primary_sources':[{'title':refs[x][0],'url':refs[x][1],'comparison_depth':refs[x][2]} for x in sources],'limitations':limits,'significance':significance,'domain_rank':rank,'rank_eligible':rank is not None,'domain_rank_rationale':significance if rank else 'Retained for complete coverage; supporting, classical, conditional, finite-certificate or failed route rather than a separately ranked main discovery.','related_ids':list(related),'priority_status':'Unresolved worldwide priority; negative search results are not novelty proof.'})
add('C02','Sharp dyadic Fourier endpoint minimax','Even the best independent row and column ordering leaves a precisely determined large cut rank.','For N=2^m≥8 in characteristic zero, min_(ρ,σ) q(Pρ F_N Pσ^T)=N/4+1, attained by double bit reversal. r_N(k)=ceil(k/2)+r_(N/4)(floor(k/2)) for k≤N/2 with reflection; total upper-cut sum is exactly minimal at N8,16 (14,48), and bit reversal has leading asymptotic N²/6.','Single-matrix exact quasiseparable rank; all independent endpoint permutations, characteristic zero.',[M+'additions/1848/ENDPOINT_AUDIT.md'],'Candidate delta is universal second-moment/odd-cardinality lower bound matching a known digit-reversal hierarchy. TW470 already gives digit-reversal rank-one grids/support uncertainty. Final2008 comparison unresolved.','No arithmetic lower bound; finite fields not covered by positivity argument; exact all-size minimum rank sum not proved.','Cleanest sharp all-size structural theorem in this census; broad intrinsic invariant and short proof. Priority risk from final Delvaux comparison prevents a first/best-known claim.',1,sources=('delvaux','delvaux_final','sampling'))
add('C01','Exact additive Green length three for C_q','A specific infinite parameter family of five-by-five matrices needs exactly three allowed Green terms.','For N=5q² with q positive odd, gcd(q,5)=1 and q≡1 mod241, the block C_q=B_N[S,S], S={0,q²,2q²,3q²,4q²}, B_N=(F_N^−1+diag(ω^((N+1)j²/2)))^−1, has exact minimum three diagonally ended Hamiltonian cyclic resolvents over a genuine quadratic extension of Q(η), η=ω^(q⁴). Upper representation has two nontrivial reciprocal-holonomy branches and one diagonal zero-weight branch.','Fixed dimension5, infinitely many arithmetic parameters. All cycle orders, legal denominators, zero edge weights and singular endpoint masks included in lower bound.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_three_green_restricted/REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_three_green_b5/REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_n5_all_orders/REVIEW.md'],'Matched exact additive length is not supplied by generic multiplicative diagonal–circulant factorization or inverse-band representation theory. Lower certificate is geometric-fiber emptiness across576 ordered pairs, not a finite rational-point scan; upper guards are uniform local-ring arguments.','Not a growing-dimensional upper family. Base-field-only upper length is unproved. Full B_N inherits only ≥3. No full uniformly cheap B_N or Fourier speedup.','Most concrete certificate-intensive additive-length novelty candidate, but specialized fixed dimension reduces breadth versus C02.',2,sources=('huhtanen','green','girs','stacks'),related=('M-CHIRP-LOWER','M-CHIRP-CUBIC'))
add('M-SEPARATOR-A','Bounded-separator inverse-sum obstruction','A flat Fourier-like unitary cannot be a constant-sized sum of independently routed inverses with small graph separators.','For complex flat unitary U, r≥1 and T=Σ_i L_i Q_i^−1 R_i with permutation-contained endpoint supports, if every required marked restriction of each symmetric bipartite support lift has a half-balanced separator≤q, U=T implies N≤4qr36^r; U=D+T implies N≤16qr36^r. Treewidth w gives q=w+1. Invertible column-two Q gives q=3, hence12r36^r/48r36^r. Fixed r,q prevent vanishing operator or normalized Frobenius error.','Exact independently routed sums, arbitrary zero endpoint weights; no row-degree restriction. Complex norm/flat-unitary comparison.',[A+'source_packages/pseudoforest_separator_independent_audit_0452/SEALED_PROOF.md',A+'source_packages/pseudoforest_separator_independent_audit_0452/PRIMARY_SOURCE_COMPARISON.md'],'Actual extension beyond inherited separation theorem is attached trees/high-degree column-two supports and general bounded vertex separators. Inverse-nullity, weighted centroid separators, GIRS and bare-cycle logarithmic bounds are antecedents. Tree witness verifies new structural coverage.','Term count≠runtime. No products/shared evaluator bound; fixed positive-error tolerance does not automatically force logarithmic r. Independent routing and bare-cycle multiplicity were already covered.','Broader target/support theorem and coherent short-note candidate using classical tools; strongest new separator-family statement, behind sharp C02 and matched C01 in this structural ranking.',3,sources=('nullity','girs','tqs','frame'),related=('M-SEPARATION','M-TREE-WITNESS','M-ROUTED-FIELD'))
add('C04','Three-stage discrepancy obstruction','Permutation discrepancy forces rank to grow in a three-stage Fourier factorization.','For F_N=S3 P2 S2 P1 S1 with q(S_i)≤r_i, arbitrary internal permutations and one affine-coprime Fourier endpoint (other arbitrary), 2r1+r2+r3≥c log N−2; transposition gives r1+r2+2r3≥c log N−2. Prime complex full spark permits both endpoints arbitrary.','Three quasiseparable stages; algebraic rank bounds in splitting fields; discrepancy of integer layouts. One-affine endpoint condition except prime complex case.',[M+'additions/2156_2159/review_three_stage/THREE_STAGE_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2213_ongoing/PRIME_ENDPOINT_COROLLARY.md'],'Reusable connection between exact cyclic-window rank inequalities and classical planar discrepancy. Classical Schmidt theorem and quasiseparable rank calculus are not new.','Not arbitrary-depth or two arbitrary non-affine composite endpoints; no explicit universal cutoff from existential c; not runtime lower bound.','Conceptual restricted-product theorem with independent significance; attractive companion to C02 but narrower endpoints.',4,sources=('schmidt','discrepancy','tao','girs'))
add('M-WEYL-BRANCH','Fixed-grammar Weyl–Green branching','Certain two-resolvent path grammars require linearly many summands to express Fourier.','Odd N: Fourier Weyl coefficient matrix has rank N. Canonical ordered G_S(α)G_T(β) with Weyl-monomial endpoints has coefficient rank≤1, so B≥N. Rotated pair U=S^uT^v,V=S^rT^s has Fourier coefficient rank N/gcd(N,δ), δ=(us−vr−ur−vs)/2. For odd prime p, any single fixed generating pair shared by all branches, without extra Weyl endpoints, needs B≥(p+1)/2.','Ordered depth-two paths in one fixed Weyl basis/pair. Canonical endpoint allowance is different from fixed-pair Hankel theorem.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_hero17_phase13/PHASE13_AUDIT.md',M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_hero17_phase13/source/hero17_phase13_weyl_branch/PROOF_CERTIFICATE.md'],'Candidate restricted grammar combination of classical Weyl/Gauss and Hankel/Vandermonde arguments. Not C05, C04 or separator A.','Changing generators can collapse coefficient rank to1. Reverse order and depth3 give full coefficient rank with O(N) application; mixed orders/generators/arbitrary diagonal gauges outside bounds.','Strong numerical branch count but narrow grammar and elementary rank mechanism; useful focused theorem or section, global priority unresolved.',5,sources=('gauss',),related=('M-MAGNETIC-SPAN',))
add('M-ROUTED-FIELD','Field-general column-two inverse-sum obstruction','The sum obstruction survives in arbitrary fields and permits attached-tree supports.','For any field with primitive Nth root, F_N=Σ_(i≤r)L_i Q_i^−1 R_i, invertible Q_i with≤2 nonzeros/column and permutation-contained endpoints, implies N≤r(r+1)^r. With row-degreeδ extra S, N≤δ(r+1)+r(r+1)^r. Two branches fail at N≥19. Any k inverse rows have exactly k independent nonzero projective column directions before endpoint masks.','Field-general exact sums, independently routed endpoints including zeros; arbitrary row degree.',[M+'additions/0431_review_and_content_extensions/routed_branch_independent_audit_0439/SEALED_PROOF.md',M+'additions/0431_review_and_content_extensions/routed_branch_independent_audit_0439/EXTENSION_AUDIT.md'],'Sharper field-general finite bound from componentwise projective directions and consecutive Fourier Vandermonde rows. Column-two/frame graph and gain-graph contraction mechanism are classical.','Weaker complex asymptotic than separation/A; not obsolete because fields and sparse-correction scope differ. No products/approximation/runtime inference.','Meaningful field/scope sibling of A with an explicit finite cutoff; keep separate rather than erase by complex norm theorem.',6,sources=('frame','nullity','girs'),related=('M-SEPARATOR-A','M-SEPARATION'))
add('M-SEPARATION','Independent-order separation-rank sum theorem','Different branch orderings still share a large low-rank rectangle.','For H_j separation ranks r_j under d distinct independent row/column order pairs, common m×m rectangle m=floor(N/2^d) has sum rank≤R=Σr_j. Flat-unitary equality requires m²≤NR; prime Fourier requires m≤R. ||U−ΣH_j||₂²≥max(0,m/N−R/m). Q rank1 branches imply Q≥0.5log₂N−O(loglogN), nearly log₂N at prime lengths.','Additive independently routed, separately gauged ordered low-rank operators; zero weights allowed. Bare multicycle blocks covered by concatenated orders.',[A+'inherited_context/ordered_separation_rank/THEOREM.md',M+'additions/2333_source_reviews/review_green_new_2307/checkpoint/SEPARATION_AND_PHASE32_REVIEW.md'],'Elementary simultaneous half-selection plus rank/norm comparison; independently routed sums and operator-error gap already established here before A.','No term-to-runtime conversion or product extension; not new GIRS theory; publication priority unresolved.','Clean substantial application and essential antecedent; lower position avoids double-counting A family as wholly independent discovery.',7,sources=('girs','tao'),related=('C05','M-SEPARATOR-A'))
add('C05','Fourier–Green one-layer obstruction','Even independently cycled Green sums plus modest corrections cannot represent large Fourier matrices.','Over C, r legal diagonally ended weighted-permutation resolvents plus rank-t, row-degree-s sparse and arbitrary diagonal corrections cannot equal F_N if N>2(m−1)(B−m)(B−1), m=r+t+1, L=m(s+2), B=(L−1)^(2^(r−1))+1. r2,t=s0 excludes N≥2301; fixed t,s force r=Ω(loglogN). Prime-factor and N4096 controls accepted.','One additive layer, independent structural cycle orders, zero edge weights, singular diagonal endpoints; no unmatched row/column routes.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_hero0_phase12/REVIEW.md'],'Combination of simultaneous monotone subsequences and positive Schur Fourier minors; nontrivial correction classes. Later separation/A strengthen overlapping core but do not explicitly subsume every sparse/low-rank correction clause.','Large nonsharp thresholds; no products or general runtime bound. Historical rank4 is not current global rank.','Historically important restricted obstruction retained with unique correction hypotheses; precursor to stronger line.',8,sources=('girs','tao','rigidity'),related=('M-SEPARATION','M-SEPARATOR-A'))
add('M-CHIRP-LOWER','Infinite forced-feedback two-Green exclusion','A finite five-point impossibility extends to infinitely many growing feedback matrices.','For positive odd q with gcd(q,5)=1 and q≡1 mod241, B_(5q²) cannot be a sum of two diagonal-ended Hamiltonian Green terms. Principal restriction preserves branch grammar including zero weights/singular masks. Positive Gauss-sign curve also gives a finite but uncomputed exceptional set for eligible N=5m, N≡1 mod4.','Forced chirp feedback B_N; fixed coordinate principal restriction, no unmatched endpoint routes.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_principal_restriction_extension/REVIEW.md'],'Proper specialization and exact square-modulus Gauss identity transfer finite geometric emptiness to growing N. Stronger than a finite N5 exclusion; C01 later adds only fixed5 upper bound.','No explicit cutoff for generic curve; negative-sign generic case unproved; does not exclude other feedback A, products or≥3 branches.','Substantial supporting infinite-family theorem within C01 package; not separately ranked to avoid double-counting.',sources=('stacks','gauss'),related=('C01','M-CHIRP-CUBIC'))
add('M-TREE-WITNESS','Uniformly conditioned tree rank-separation witness','Small-separator inverse matrices can require growing cut rank under every independent ordering.','For perfect binary tree height h, N=2^(h+1)−1, Q=I−P, floor((h+1)/4)≤sr(Q^−1)=sr(Q)≤h over every field. Lift is subcubic tree, q2. Q_(h,α)=I−αP preserves exact ranks; over C,0<α<1/sqrt2 gives κ₂≤(1+αsqrt2)/(1−αsqrt2), and α1/2 yields3+2sqrt2<6.','sr minimizes both cut orientations over independent row and column permutations; numerical-rank tolerance not included.',[A+'source_packages/tree_rank_separation_audit_0548/PROOF_AUDIT.md',A+'source_packages/tree_rank_separation_audit_0548/CONDITIONING_AUDIT.md'],'Closes precise A non-containment gate with an independent-axis bridge. Nullity, forest matching, pathwidth and binary-tree precedent in final2025 TQS are classical.','Does not prove reverse containment/proper-superset relation, optimal SSS/HSS storage, or fixed-tolerance numerical rank. Not resolution of a published TQS open question.','Useful attributed supporting proposition, not standalone graph-width breakthrough.',sources=('tqs','forest','nullity'),related=('M-SEPARATOR-A',))
add('C07','Two-sided rectangle rank oracle','An exact graph oracle and moving cuts can certify impossible Green products.','rank K^−1[A,B]=|A|+|B|−N+rank K[B^c,A^c]; for legal cyclic Green denominator complementary support paths permit O(N) matching oracle. Moving interfaces bound rank(AB)[R,C] by rank B[S,C]+rank A[R,S^c]. Two-stage objective is submodular. N64 witness improves fixed budget34 to moving budget4 versus target rank16, yielding operator error≥1.','Supports/routes/masks explicitly tracked; one oracle/certificate linear, optimization polynomial via known methods.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_two_sided_green/REVIEW.md'],'Useful exact specialized synthesis of nullity, matching, Fourier coset spectra and matroid/submodular tools. Core identities known.','Passing cuts not sufficient; singular endpoint exact rank requires supported-coordinate deletion; no linear-time optimizer or full evaluator.','Reusable certification framework with scope advantages, supporting rather than primary novelty claim.',sources=('nullity','girs','submodular'))
add('C09','Exact sixteen-point Green coefficient certificate','A fixed sixteen-point architecture really represents Fourier exactly, beyond a numerical fit.','F16=H2 H1 B H0 with8 fixed Hamiltonian routes/poles per layer,24 branch occurrences,384 complex endpoint entries. Exact rational contraction isolates unique root in256-dimensional affine chart, radius10^−9, all256 equations and384 nonzero guards.','Finite complex algebraic existence; uniqueness within chart only.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_n16_contraction/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Exact specific witness replaces floating residual; rational root certification is established.','Overparameterized finite seed; no size lift/uniform generator/complexity gain; positive certificate means existence, not positive real coefficients.','Valuable reproducible benchmark or appendix, not main all-size discovery.',sources=('alpha','huhtanen'))
add('C10','Projective row-constraint graph solver','A two-Green necessary subsystem can be decided without exponential branch enumeration.','Bilinear P1 constraints u_k^T L_e u_i=0: rank2 edges transport directions; cycles yield all P1,≤2 points or empty; rank1 edges give equality disjunctions/2-SAT. Includes infinity, repeated roots,char2 and algebraic-closure gcd decisions. Conservative polynomial extraction/solver cost.','Selected necessary row subsystem; base-field root costs separate.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_projective_graph/REVIEW.md'],'Complex core directly overlaps quantum2SAT transfer-matrix/cycle/singular-edge methods; potential field-general and Green-extraction implementation delta only.','Success does not solve columns, scales or full factorization. General solver novelty must not be claimed.','Accepted mathematics, clearly downgraded novelty; retain as attributed tool.',sources=('quantum','quantum2'))
add('C11','Sparse-inverse and low-rank product gates','Classical uncertainty bounds rule out certain sparse-plus-low-rank stage products.','If F=ΠH_i, invertible H_i=G_i+R_i, rankR_i≤r_i and G_i^−1 column sparsity≤s_i, then s(r+1)²≥N for r=Σr_i,s=Πs_i; prime complex variant(s+1)(r+1)≥p+1. Row-sparse rigidity also yields rank(F−S)≥floor(N/(s+1)), not N−s.','Restricted inverse-sparsity/low-rank corrections; cost consequences need explicit fully materialized executor.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_hero17_phase12/PHASE12_AUDIT.md',M+'additions/0431_review_and_content_extensions/green_geometry_source_review_0430/PROOF_AND_SCOPE.md'],'Clean reusable corollaries of inverse-difference telescoping, sparse null vectors and classical uncertainty.','No universal FFT lower bound; finite-field additive uncertainty not imported from prime complex case; dense structured repairs remain possible.','Supporting known-mechanism lemma, unranked as original discovery.',sources=('tao','rigidity'))
add('C13-FIXED-DIRECTIONS','Fixed-direction Green completion','Once all projective directions are supplied, remaining feasibility reduces to guarded affine scale equations.','Full off-support vanishing and UBV=U D_y+D_x V, nonzero scales/base coordinates and legal cycle guards are necessary/sufficient for invertible branch completion with fixed routes. Complete off-support check costs O(N²); supported affine graph solve linear field work with finite-field exclusion checks.','Directions/routes fixed; singular-endpoint boundary has necessity but no converse here.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_fixed_direction_completion/REVIEW.md'],'Useful exact application/guard ledger; affine graph propagation and projective recovery established.','Does not solve direction discovery; direction-pass/scale-failure explicit N5 control; finite fields need enough nonzero scale choices.','Methods appendix, unranked; C13 fixed-pencil exclusions delegated to algebra catalogue.',sources=('quantum','quantum2'))
add('M-TWO-STAGE','Boundary-window two-stage exclusion','Two low-cut-rank stages cannot realize Fourier beyond a small explicit size.','For T=S2 P S1, R=r1+r2 and relevant two boundary target blocks full rank W=floor(N/2), N≤4R+1. Two order1 stages fail N≥10 with one affine-coprime Fourier endpoint; prime complex N≥11 permits arbitrary endpoints.','Full quasiseparable class including singular stages/zero transitions; one internal arbitrary permutation.',[M+'additions/2213_ongoing/review_two_green_v17/TWO_STAGE_BOUNDARY_EXTENSION.md',M+'additions/2213_ongoing/review_two_green_v17/V17_AUDIT.md'],'Boundary windows strengthen older N17/N31 gates and remove separated-generator genericity assumptions using elementary rank calculus.','No existence below threshold; no general algorithm bound or arbitrary composite endpoint claim.','Useful explicit strengthening within obstruction toolkit; main novelty better grouped with C04.',sources=('tao','girs'),related=('C04','C02'))
add('M-AFFINE-STEP','Simultaneous affine-step Green product obstruction','Products can be ruled out when all routed cycle steps have bounded affine complexity.','For dyadic N, products/sums of Green branches with≤d step magnitudes and≤b exceptional edges per occurrence, affine intermediate routing and arbitrary diagonals, total occurrences Q=Ω(logN/loglogN). Holds also fixed complex operator error ε<1/sqrt2. Certified common balanced character-cut rank≤T floor((N−1)/r)+Σfloor(b_q/2), r=floor((N−1)^(1/s)).','Occurrence-counted expression tree, bounded transformed step complexity, no free DAG reuse; complex approximation comparison.',[M+'additions/1930_phase26/PHASE26_AUDIT.md'],'Nontrivial simultaneous Diophantine-cut application to restricted products, with factor-two crossing improvement. Different model from additive separation.','Arbitrary non-affine routing escapes; term count not scalar work; exact strict-cut implementation correction retained.','Infinite restricted-product result worth retaining below main candidates; bounded prior-art search only.',9,sources=('girs',),related=('M-SEPARATION','C04'))
add('M-PARITY-DEPTH','Parity Fourier ranks and affine scan depth','Binary-affine routing cannot indefinitely hide all low-boundary cuts.','N2^k, parity halfsets with mask highest bits u,v have exact complex Fourier rank N/4 if u+v≤k−2 and N/2 otherwise. For quasiseparable orders r_j and GF2-affine internal routing, quotas q_j≥1 with Σr_j2^−q_j≤1/4 force Σq_j≥k; uniform r gives k≤t ceil(log₂(4rt)).','Complex rank; arbitrary external invertible monomials permitted by flat-unitary bound; GF2-affine internals essential.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_parity_affine/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Parity-rank application and moving-mask dimension argument build on classical universal sampling; stage-depth growth different from total arithmetic.','No arbitrary nonlinear routing theorem; source uniform capacity helper missing r weight for r>1, saved r1 witnesses unaffected.','Useful exact oracle plus restricted depth theorem; potential technical note, not general lower bound.',10,sources=('sampling',),related=('M-NONLINEAR-ROUTING',))
add('M-CHORD','Chord-rigidity sparse-sandwich bound','Odd-polygon geometry sharply limits cancellation in a restricted Fourier sandwich.','Over C, primitive-affine three-frequency profiles and Hamiltonian right cycle imply adjacent-row union support≥n−2, locally sharp for every odd n≥5. Hence nnz≥ceil(n(n−2)/2); scalar-polynomial bridge degree L must satisfy4^(L+1)≥1+(n−2)/6.','Complex odd roots; external extended-line incidence theorem; fixed sparse sandwich/bridge grammar.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_chord_rigidity/REVIEW.md'],'Interesting geometric application, but the central polygon-incidence input is attributed and original Rigby comparison remains unresolved.','Near-full bound false over finite fields (F19,N9 counterexample); polynomial-degree obstruction not arbitrary fast solve; arbitrary non-affine composite triples outside scope.','Potential specialized synthesis; left unranked conditional on the uncompleted primary dependency comparison.',status='conditional: matrix deductions accepted given stated published odd-polygon incidence theorem',sources=('rigby','tao'))
add('M-FCUT','Fourier-cycle sparse-sandwich density','A certain sparse sandwich around Fourier must still contain quadratically many nonzeros.','At prime p≥3, arbitrary Hamiltonian cycles and complex weights with invertible monomial endpoints give every adjacent-row support union≥ceil(p/2), hence nnz≥ceil(p ceil(p/2)/2). Denominator invertibility unnecessary for density. Primitive-affine triples extend local argument to composite lengths.','Sparse sandwich density; prime complex full-spark or explicitly primitive-stride triples.',[M+'additions/2213_ongoing/review_fcut/FCUT_AUDIT.md'],'Quantitative density is additional; prime p≥11 two-resolvent exclusion overlaps prior separator/v17. Classical propagation and full spark.','Dense center can be fast; no quadratic work lower bound; arbitrary composite non-affine triples not covered.','Useful subordinate density theorem; not ranked above broader additive results.',sources=('tao',),related=('M-CHORD','M-SEPARATION'))
add('M-NONLINEAR-ROUTING','Moving-set and nonlinear-routing gates','Exact rank tests extend to selected nonlinear routing changes, without ruling out all nonlinear designs.','Periodic full-spark input columns C={e+hj} give rank F_N[R,C]=Σρ min(nρ,m). Arbitrary transported sets obey rank product[A_t^c,A_1]≤Σr_j d(A_j). Routing edits add≤Σrank(P_j−A_j); permutation edit rank=N−number of relative cycles. Modified N256 has rank128>capacity124; pinned N2048/N4096 two-Toffoli variants fail.','Specified quasiseparable stage layouts; periodic/full-spark oracle columns; exact field rank vs complex universal sampling distinguished.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_nonlinear_rank_gate/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Useful nonlinear-route extension and explicit obstruction certificates built from classical rank telescoping/sampling.','Original N256 still survives these tests; no arbitrary nonlinear-routing exclusion; high permutation edit rank can have O(N) execution.','Subordinate structural/certificate family.',sources=('sampling','girs'),related=('M-PARITY-DEPTH','M-EXPANDER-COEFFICIENT'))
add('M-NONLINEAR-COMPATIBILITY','All cuts can pass while coefficient compatibility fails generically','Network capacity cannot certify realizability of a particular matrix.','Fixed N8 two-stage rank1 separated-generator graph has maximum flow for all12869 equal-size terminal pairs, but matrix image dimension exactly60<64. General t-stage rank-r chart dimension≤min(n²,n+2tr(2n−2r−1)); arbitrary fixed permutations/diagonal phases do not enlarge it. N16 tangent witness remains finite-field first-order only.','Separated-generator polynomial chart, not all quasiseparable representations; generic target theorem.',[M+'nonlinear/NONLINEAR_INDEPENDENT_AUDIT.md'],'Concrete strict separation of graph cut capacity from coefficient-image dimension; gauge dimension count classical.','Does not prove Fourier outside image. All-r macro-to-ordered-scan lifting shortcut refuted, global lifted-superconcentrator conjecture open.','Useful methodological counterexample and finite certificate, no main Fourier lower-bound novelty.',sources=('girs','huhtanen'))
add('M-F8-EXACT','Exact eight-point three-stage certificate','A small three-stage Fourier factorization exists exactly.','Normalized F8=S3 P S2 P S1 with repeated bit reversal and separated-generator order1 stages. Rational contraction on64 complex variables with56 frozen parameters, radius2^−30, contraction<0.027855 isolates exact solution.','Fixed N8 complex algebraic root certificate.',[M+'additions/2213_ongoing/review_f8_certificate/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Specific rigorous existence beyond optimizer residual; contraction technique established.','No closed-form/uniform coefficients or all-size lift; compatible with larger-size exclusions.','Finite positive benchmark; unranked.',sources=('alpha',),related=('C09','C04'))
add('M-FIXED-BITREV','Repeated-bit-reversal finite and uniform cut obstructions','A particular repeated bit-reversal scan layout fails from explicit sizes.','Three order1 stages: source uniform cut for N=32m≥64 has13m-square full-rank Fourier block but12m+1 wires. Four stages at N2048: rank683 versus cut676. General repeated-layout growth results retained in source lineage.','Fixed scalar scan graph/layout and declared state dimensions; coefficients arbitrary within graph.',[M+'additions/2213_ongoing/three_stage/approved_bitrev64_source_milestone/AUDIT.md',M+'additions/0431_review_and_content_extensions/green_geometry_source_review_0430/PROOF_AND_SCOPE.md'],'Explicit cut certificates sharpen N128 result, not arbitrary-layout theorem.','No universal four-stage exclusion; missing communication/state not represented by graph outside theorem.','Accepted finite/uniform layout certificates, subordinate to discrepancy/depth family.',sources=('girs',),related=('C04','M-PARITY-DEPTH'))
add('M-FOURIER4-GREEN','Small exact Fourier Green kernels','Several four-point Green constructions are exact but do not lift automatically.','One paired-Green F4 kernel exists over fields with primitive eighth root and a distinct-root quadratic guard. Separate Phase16 exact F4 factorization uses two four-Green sums with12 zero edge occurrences and escapes common constant-reference gauge; local s2 rook decomposition valid.','Fixed N4; algebraic extensions and root setup explicitly required; zero masks allowed.',[M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/remaining_bank_certificates_audit/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_hero0_phase16_gauge_curvature/REVIEW.md'],'Useful exact seed/control, mechanisms are chirp interpolation and elementary quadratic decomposition.','No optimal Green length, all-nonzero holonomy certificate or growing-size algorithm; constant-size kernels cannot be silently promoted.','Finite construction/certificate family; unranked.',sources=('huhtanen','gauss'))
add('M-F8-ORBIT','Eight-point anchor and orbit exclusions','Several prescribed Fourier8 support charts are rigorously impossible.','Eight stipulated anchor charts excluded under recorded guards; entire half-pair anchor nonsingular diagonal orbit excluded over characteristic≠2 with primitive eighth root. Adjacent guarded chart has40 equations in12 variables; later boundary/full-orbit exclusion subsumed by classical cut-rank proof.','Fixed support cycles and anchors; zero-pivot/zero-edge boundaries handled where explicitly audited.',[M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/remaining_bank_certificates_audit/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0322_exact_code_and_chirp_results/fourier8_orbit_independent_audit_0312/AUDIT_VERDICT.md',M+'additions/0400_review_and_infinite_families/scoped_theorem_priority_0407/CUT_RANK_PROOF.md'],'Exact exported polynomial/ideal certificates preserved. Adjacent orbit needs no new obstruction technique: inverse cut rank≤3 versus Fourier rank4 is stronger and simpler.','Not universal F8/two-layer impossibility; some older charts require nonsingular endpoints; numerical failed searches prove nothing.','Known-method finite exclusions, unranked.',sources=('girs','nullity'),related=('C13-FIXED-DIRECTIONS',))
add('M-CHIRP-CUBIC','Odd-chirp cubic feedback identity','A cheap chirp gives an exact small-degree feedback specification, but its companion operator is still expensive or unknown.','Odd N, primitiveω,char∤2N, A_jj=ω^((N+1)j²/2),G=ΣA_jj,c=NG: (FA)^3=cI; exact degree3 for N≥5. Under1+c≠0, B=(F^−1+A)^−1 and K=BA obey K³−c(1−K)³=0, (I−K)^−1=(1+c)I+(1−2c)K+(1+c)K².','All odd splitting-field lengths; complex unnormalized case automatically nonresonant, finite-field resonance possible.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_chirp_feedback/REVIEW.md'],'Direct convention-correct Gauss/Weil cubic identity and guarded feedback reformulation; classical spectral ingredients.','A cheap; B formula contains Fourier and is not a fast construction. Exact F5 recovery has6 nontrivial solves, constant-size only.','Supporting identity with unresolved constructive premise, not a new FFT.',sources=('gauss',),related=('C01','M-CHIRP-LOWER'))
add('M-QUADRATIC-FEEDBACK','Cheap quadratic feedback and its Fourier obstruction','Low loop degree and a correct seed are insufficient to obtain Fourier.','Even N common weighted Hamiltonian W, alternating E, Cayleys C_a,C_b and A=C_a,B=λC_b E give exact minimal polynomial(BA)²−λ²I and O(N) evaluator. Fourier covariance forces N≤9; a0/b0 branches N≤4, a=±b branches N≤6. A separate all-even construction meets seed but fails covariance.','Common-cycle paired-Green subclass; legal Cayley/nonresonance guards; field support-product uncertainty.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_feedback_annihilator_family/REVIEW.md'],'Explicit cheap positive closure plus all-parameter subclass exclusion; classical support uncertainty/Cayley algebra.','Not independently ordered general feedback no-go; root/bit/conditioning costs separate.','Useful negative control isolating missing phase compatibility, unranked.',sources=('tao',))
add('M-SPECTRAL-FEEDBACK','Quadratic spectral feedback characterization','A feedback search can be reformulated as a two-eigenvalue condition, without solving synthesis.','For λ≠0,λ²≠1, M=FA must satisfy M²−sM+pI=0, s=−2p, p=−λ²/(1−λ²), and prescribed projector rank to be similar to required two-eigenvalue diagonal. Forced B formulas follow. Fixed N4 two-amplitude noncommuting ansatz excluded by exact nonzero6×6 coefficient minor.','Splitting field char∤2N; integer projector rank, not trace alone, in positive characteristic.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_spectral_feedback/REVIEW.md'],'Exact characterization/guard ledger from elementary spectral algebra; finite rejection is specific.','No cheap conjugator, admissible positive A/B or uniformly cheap inverse. Fourier-oracle controls not constructions.','Classical reduction plus finite certificate; unranked.',sources=('gauss',),related=('M-QUADRATIC-FEEDBACK',))
add('M-CONJUGATED-FEEDBACK','Noncommuting conjugated-involution control','Noncommuting cheap factors can enforce quadratic closure but still fail Fourier.','BA=λCJC^−1 implies transfer CΔC^−1 A^−1. Direct independent-Cayley ansatz closes iff the Cayleys commute. Explicit even-N noncommuting conjugated construction has quadratic closure and constant scan composition, but fixed cut rank≤5 excludes Fourier for N≥12.','Known actions/inverses and lawful denominators; specified common parity/cycle routes.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_conjugated_feedback/REVIEW.md'],'Clarifies equivalence and separate synthesis/cost obligations; elementary commutator and cut-rank argument.','Five-factor supplied B representation does not prove B outside all two-Green representations. No Fourier-compatible factorization.','Supporting control; unranked.',sources=('nullity','girs'))
add('M-NILPOTENT-FOLD','All-scalar Fourier folding obstruction','Simply copying smaller layers into four fibers cannot build the larger Fourier transform.','For specified four-to-one rectangular/square fold Q and compatible roots, QF_(4N)−γF_NQ has full row rankN for everyγ over splitting fields char∤4N. A selected minor equals det(F_N)(−γ)^N using nilpotence;γ0 handled separately. Proper active bank gives layer-defect rank sum≥N−b|J|.','Exact specified fold, bank position and scalar-copy layers; arbitrary scalar normalization included.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_nilpotent_fold_addendum/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Nontrivial exact nilpotent minor strengthening of an earlier norm-gap gate; closes normalization escape only for this lift.','Genuine four-fiber mixing/changed banks outside model; rank defect easily generated in O(N), not cost lower bound.','Useful project-specific all-size obstruction, potential supporting lemma.',sources=('nullity',),related=('M-MGG-CAPACITY',))
add('M-MGG-CAPACITY','Hamiltonian expander capacity escape','Explicit cycle banks defeat one important family of rank tests without realizing Fourier.','Every dyadic N≥2^17 admits8 O(N)-enumerable Hamiltonian cycles with three-copy aggregate incoming capacity>N/2 on every balanced common subset. Hierarchical exact edit count multiplies by4; margins768·4^ℓ and15360·4^ℓ for certified seeds.','MGG square/rectangular quotient and splicing; common-subset complementary edge counts only.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_nonlinear_cycle_bank/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_nilpotent_fold_addendum/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Concrete low-edit Hamiltonianization of classical expander support, with exact arithmetic capacity margins.','No moving-interface separator sufficiency, actual rank attainment, phase coefficients, compatible full Fourier lift or cost advantage.','Accepted topology construction only; unranked as Fourier discovery.',sources=('expander',))
add('M-EXPANDER-COEFFICIENT','Expansion survives but nonlinear coefficient equations remain','An exact expanding layout can exhaust its boundary tests while still face strong coefficient conditions.','Pinned N256 four-path affine Laplacian hasλ2>101/50 via exact rational congruence/diagonal dominance. Therefore transported boundary-sum test cannot reject any target. Fourier realization still requires a128-square transformed block rank≤16; identity outer inverses give rank128. Separate fourth-moment enclosure givesσ17>3sqrt2/5.','One fixed four-stage common-order layout; outer-inverse nonlinear compatibility.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_expander_coefficient_gate/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/INTEGRATED_RESULTS.md'],'Exact finite graph and spectral/coefficient certificates distinguish capacity from synthesis.','Not a full-network separator theorem or feasible coefficient solution; strong finite evidence does not produce uniform construction.','Finite test-method boundary, unranked.',sources=('girs','alpha'),related=('M-NONLINEAR-ROUTING','M-NONLINEAR-COMPATIBILITY'))
add('M-CUT-EXPANDER','Graph-cut rank bounds and all-cut capacity survivors','Some expander networks pass every same-set capacity test and still need phase compatibility.','Fixed-coordinate Green sums/products rank bounded by total nonzero crossing occurrences, counting inserted permutations. Flat-unitary blocks yield explicit Frobenius/operator error floors. Classical MGG20-plan two-stage all-square topology exceeds maximal cut capacity. Lifted block compatibility gives rankH(F)=(r+s)N+rank(F−YX).','Fixed coordinate grammar, arbitrary-permutation multi-cycle plans;20 plans broader than four-Hamiltonian grammar.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_hero0_phase13/REVIEW.md'],'Corrected cut accounting and explicit capacity-only construction; rank/nullity/expansion ingredients established.','Capacity survivor not Fourier identity; actual rank may cancel; shuffles cannot be free.','Supporting graph framework, unranked.',sources=('girs','expander'),related=('M-TRANSVERSE','M-WEYL-TWIRL'))
add('M-TRANSVERSE','Transverse-rank obstruction despite expansion','All ordinary graph cuts can pass while a two-axis circuit stays far from Fourier.','For N=s², paths YX with X preserving y and Y preserving x have each transverse block rank≤1; sum r paths has error relativeFrobenius≥sqrt(1−r/s), operator≥sqrt(1−r/s). s paths suffice in enlarged arbitrary-fiber grammar. Classical Cartesian expander40-plan network passes all same-subset capacities but retains r1 obstruction.','Polarized two-axis order, no extra axis switching/unaccounted routing; complex approximation.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_hero0_phase14/REVIEW.md'],'Sharp restricted path count plus infinite capacity-counterfamily is meaningful synthesis of elementary tensor cuts and classical expanders.','No mixed-axis Phase13 exclusion; generic rook dimension count is not Fourier-specific; branch count≠runtime.','One of stronger supporting restricted-model separations; potentially a useful section.',sources=('expander','girs'))
add('M-SYMMETRY','Weyl symmetry and gauge-rigidity gates','Preserved symmetries force explicit approximation gaps, and editing too few weight occurrences cannot fix them.','Half-grid-invariant Margulis Green networks commute with chosen involutions at all depths. Exact Fourier commutator spectra give sharp commutant distance1 or cos(pi/8), joint relativeFrobenius sqrt3/2. k occurrence-wise weight edits satisfy rank(T−T0)≤k, so exact breaking requires k≥N/4 or N/2. Phase16 common diagonal gauge inherits symmetry; single Green beside rook support fails s≥3.','Legal symmetric reference and occurrence-wise counts; common gauge constants/nonzero edge premise where used.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_hero0_phase15/REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_hero0_phase16_gauge_curvature/REVIEW.md'],'Explicit spectra/sharp constants and scoped gauge support tests; classical commutant projection, low-rank perturbation and graph holonomy mechanics.','O(N) edits still O(N) work; arbitrary weights/routes not excluded; forest residual count not canonical minimum edit count.','Supporting symmetry family with exact constants, unranked.',sources=('gauss','girs'))
add('M-WEYL-RESIDUAL','Sharp Weyl residual certificate','Two covariance equations certify Fourier and quantify residual distance in a stated model.','Calibrated MZ=DM and MD=Z^−1M imply M=F. Joint Frobenius residual distance to scalar Fourier family has sharp gap2sin(pi/N). Fixed linear finite-field oracle:1+3h calls yields exact false acceptance p^(−hρ),ρ rank stacked defects.','Fixed input-independent linear map, exact roots/field and independent uniform probes; normalized complex metric separate.',[M+'additions/1717/phase20_audit/PHASE20_AUDIT.md'],'Convention-correct sharp certificate from classical Weyl diagonalization; project verifier implementation, not new transform.','Gap decays with N; finite random passes not identity proof; adaptive/stateful oracle not covered; specialization guards for complex rejection.','Useful verifier and sharp constant, unranked.',sources=('gauss',))
add('M-SPARSE-DEFECT','Sparse inverse and commutator approximation floors','Specific sparse or nearly commuting matrices remain quantitatively far from Fourier.','Any inverse row of support≤s gives ||M−F||₂≥sqrt(1−s/N). rank[M,Z]≤r gives bound cos((2floor(r/2)+1)π/(2N)). For B with columns≤s, ||ZB−BD||F≥2sin(π/(2(s+1)))||B||F, sharp via sine vector.','Unitary complex Fourier and specified inverse-support/commutator architecture.',[M+'additions/1717/phase20_audit/PHASE20_AUDIT.md'],'Sharper explicit bounds from uncertainty, Dirichlet path spectrum and commutator singular values.','Sums may have dense inverses; variable phases/routes defeat low commutator premises; no universal runtime bound.','Scoped quantitative supporting theorem, unranked.',sources=('gauss','tao'))
add('M-WEYL-TWIRL','Weyl twirl certification and rejected shuffle extension','A randomized symmetry loss measures distance to Fourier, but one advertised cut extension was false.','Exact Weyl twirl average half residualFrobenius²=minλ||M−λU||F²; four-phase probes retain second moment≤8τ⁴ and dimension-independent sampling counts. Seed calibrates scalar. Fixed-cut Green calculus accepted. Source uncharged interstage-shuffle claim refuted at N12 by half-swap between identity stages.','Fixed candidate; exact/discrete sampling model; fixed-frame cuts with all routing charged.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_weyl_expansion/REVIEW.md'],'Classical twirl projected into useful evaluator testing; explicit counterexample corrects overreach.','No optimization convergence/uniform synthesis guarantee; corrected gauge/route bookkeeping required; random low loss not exact equality.','Accepted tool plus refuted extension; unranked.',sources=('gauss','girs','ailon'))
add('M-MAGNETIC-SPAN','Signed magnetic Green span and nearest-neighbor depth','The span of four magnetic resolvent families has an exact even-length missing mode.','Over C four signed families(I−αS^ε−βT^δ)^−1 span allN² Weyl positions for oddN, and all except(N/2,N/2) for evenN. Fourier belongs iff4∤N. Corrected true-partition nearest-neighbor path bound ΣL_b≥floor(N/2).','Ungauged signed families in fixed generators; legalΔ=1−α^N−β^N; nearest-neighbor path grammar.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_hero17_phase14/PHASE14_AUDIT.md'],'Exact signed support classification and missing Fourier coefficient; root-of-unity q-binomial identity is classical.','Existential span≠cheap synthesis; Weyl endpoints/long stride/products escape. Original odd equal-half product-rank lemma false (N3 counterexample), repaired theorem accepted.','Useful distinct restricted representation classification; unranked pending focused priority comparison.',sources=('gauss',),related=('M-WEYL-BRANCH',))
