add('M-TENSOR-CUT','Four-leg Fourier tensor ranks and local sparse-core rigidity','A sparse tensor core only appears after paying for local Fourier changes of basis.','For N=QM, T[s,h,t,u]=ω^(−ht)ξ^(−st)η^(−hu) has three paired flattening ranks N,min(Q,M),N and CP rank N. Under separate invertible changes on the s and u legs, support≥N, with equality iff the two transformed endpoint Fourier matrices are monomial.','Four individual digit legs, specified flattenings and endpoint-local gauges.',[M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_incoming_2257_routed/SOURCE_REVIEW.md'],'Exact rank/gauge classification; standard tensor flattenings and Vandermonde proofs.','Joint two-leg changes, other realignment ranks and arbitrary arithmetic circuits excluded; min(Q,M) must grow for fixed-width exclusion.','Useful explanatory synthesis; unranked.',sources=('delvaux','gauss'))
add('M-RECTANGLE-TILING','Exact rank-one Fourier rectangle tiling optimum','Literal rank-one rectangle decompositions have an exact support-incidence cost.','A Fourier rectangle is rank one iff N divides every product of a row difference and column difference. Each lies in a coset/annihilator-coset rectangle, area≤N. The minimum disjoint rank-one rectangle incidence cost is N min_(d|N)(d+N/d), equal2N^(3/2) at square N and N(N+1) at prime N.','Literal rectangle tilings and independent dense rank-factor implementations.',[M+'additions/2333_source_reviews/review_hero17_phase7/PHASE7_AUDIT.md'],'Sharp finite combinatorial optimization in fixed cost model using classical Fourier subgroup geometry.','Shared Cooley–Tukey computation avoids literal cost; nonsquare-composite higher-rank optimum not proved.','Supporting exact optimum, not generic arithmetic lower bound.',sources=('delvaux','tao'))
add('M-HARPER','Parity-resolved Harper polynomial depth','Fourier cannot be a scalar function of one standard Harper operator, but its two parity pieces have exact polynomial degrees.','For N divisible4, periodic H=Z+Z^−1+D+D^−1 has two zero modes with distinct Fourier eigenvalues. Thus F≠f(H). In parity resolution F=p_+(H)(I+J)/2+p_−(H)(I−J)/2, exact degrees are N/2 and N/2−2, with leading even coefficient1/(2sqrtN). Fixed-stage dual Weyl gauge equations reduce to simultaneous monomial similarity and graph cocycles.','Complex normalized Fourier; one commuting Harper functional calculus; fixed-stage gauges.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_phase_pencil/source/PRIOR_PHASE18_THEOREM.md',M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_phase_pencil/source/PRIOR_PHASE19_THEOREM.md',M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_phase_pencil/REVIEW.md'],'Harper duality/zero modes are explicitly classical; exact parity degrees and leading coefficient are specialized refinements.','Source proof read; attached saved audit is for downstream gauge gate, not independent replay of every Harper finite certificate. General noncommuting functional calculus untouched.','Supporting known-plus-refinement row, unranked.',status='source proof inspected; inherited internal acceptance, no separate current replay',sources=('gauss',))
add('M-FOUR-STAGE-COLLAPSE','Four-stage bounded-fragmentation collapse','A low-crossing middle permutation does not create an unrestricted new four-stage architecture.','For middle multiplication-by3, q(S3 Q S2 Q^−1)≤r3+5r2, so three-stage discrepancy gives2r1+r3+5r2+r4≥c logN−2. Saved bitrev–multiply3–bitrev rank-one layout fails for dyadic N≥2^27. General middle fragmentation yields analogous merged-order bound.','Four QS stages; exact middle ordering and endpoint hypotheses inherited from three-stage theorem.',[M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_affine_middle/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Restricted composition application of discrepancy theorem.','Not arbitrary middle permutations; explicit cutoff is conservative; no circuit bound.','Subordinate to C04.',sources=('girs','discrepancy'),related=('C04',))
add('M-REPEATED-BITREV','Repeated-bit-reversal central-cut depth barrier','Reusing bit reversal has a growing-order requirement visible at one central cut.','For k-bit indices with preserved/swapped central partition, N/2≤d_N Σr_i, where d_N=2^((k+1)/2)−1 for odd k and2^(k/2) for even k. Thus total QS orderΩ(sqrtN); four rank-one stages fail for N≥128.','Repeated bit-reversal stage grammar, primitive-root fields; exact central four Fourier blocks.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_repeated_bitrev_depth/REPEATED_BITREV_AUDIT.md'],'All-depth extension of fixed-stage witnesses, elementary rank/cut mechanism.','Other routing can move the central partition; depth/order is not runtime.','Subordinate structural strengthening.',sources=('girs','delvaux'),related=('M-FIXED-BITREV',))
add('M-MOVING-SPARSE','Moving-interface sparse-reference inverse gate','Sparse inverse baselines plus low-rank errors remain constrained even when the internal partitions move.','If each inverse factor is row-d_j-sparse plus rank-r_j error, full inverse is row-Πd_j-sparse plus rank≤Σr_j error. Fourier requires floor(N/(Πd_j+1))≤Σr_j. Moving twisted bit-reversal carries corresponding sqrt-depth gates.','Products of fixed linear factors, charged routing and exact Fourier.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_phase34_moving_weyl/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Telescoping extension of standard sparse Fourier rank lemma.','No bound from sparse-baseline degrees when factors are additive sums with dense inverses; zero-parameter support degeneracy explicitly retained.','Supporting gate, unranked.',sources=('girs','tao'),related=('C11','M-REPEATED-BITREV'))
add('M-STRIPED-BANK','Striped-bank and balanced-separator product bounds','Preserving selected bank partitions forces many paired Green factors.','Dyadic N, m=2^floor(log2(N)/2),q=N/m: product with L weighted Green occurrences in cycles Z and RZR, bank-block-preserving endpoints and arbitrary block-diagonal banks obeys L(q/2+m)≥N/2. Hence L≥ceil(N/(q+2m)); three fail≥128,four≥256. Balanced/complement rectangle method supplies companion geometry-specific separator bounds.','Paired cycles and partition-preserving bank grammar.',[M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_recursive_bank/STRIPED_CUT_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2333_source_reviews/review_routed_green_products/area_separator_audit/REVIEW.md'],'Explicit full-rank striped Fourier block applied to routed bank grammar.','Not arbitrary bank routing or sums; companion balanced-bound constants not promoted beyond saved audit.','Supporting growing-depth restriction.',sources=('girs','delvaux'))
add('M-ALL-STAGE-SUBSETS','All stage-subset diagonal-defect inequalities at N256','Every subset of stages in one surviving layout must carry substantial ordinary rank away from diagonals.','For the saved four-QS1 affine N256 layout, every diagonal baseline, including singular, obeys15 subset inequalities: singleton38,44,69,46; pair119,118,112,109,95,105; each triple127; allfour128. Sumh≥234, optimal within this15-inequality relaxation, witnessed by(70,49,69,46).','Fixed saved affine layout;255 parity coordinate masks, not all coordinate subsets.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_all_subsets_rigidity/REVIEW.md'],'Exact finite simultaneous-mask strengthening beyond one boundary test.','Rank234 not arithmetic work: a single linear-time scan can have diagonal-defect rankN−1. Relaxation witness is not Fourier factors.','Finite support certificate, unranked.',sources=('girs',),related=('M-EXPANDER-COEFFICIENT',))
add('M-PHASE-PENCIL','Fixed-stage two-column phase pencil','A phase equation can reject every allowed middle diagonal even when the network has excess rank capacity.','For invertible fixed A,B, F=L A diag(d)B with nonzero d iff all covariance pencils K_j d=0, with invertibility giving nonzero output row scales. detK0≠0 suffices to reject; singularK0 not sufficient. Explicit four-Green N8 has detK0=55687 mod65537 and every12,869 nonempty square minor nonzero, with guarded characteristic-zero nonvanishing lift.','Fixed stage data and Fourier ordering; middle/output diagonals, not arbitrary newly variable endpoints.',[M+'additions/0155_material_coverage_and_new_results/reviews/review_phase_pencil/REVIEW.md'],'Concrete coefficient incompatibility certificate beyond one-sided min-cut capacity; graph diagonal similarity and generic matroid rank classical.','The witness does NOT defeat all rank tests: Fourier minor rows{0,4},cols{0,2} rank1 but candidate rank2. Forming dense pencils/determinant not shown linear time.','Useful finite separation of capacity from phase compatibility, unranked.',sources=('girs',),related=('M-NONLINEAR-COMPATIBILITY',))
add('M-POSITIVE-PHASE','Positive-middle calibration and phase-rank gate','Matching Fourier’s first row and column does not fix its complex phases.','Two positive masks calibrate the first cross by classical matrix scaling. If entrywise phase matrix has rank≤r, ||F−T||F≥sqrt(N−r)/2. Positive middle with arbitrary complex internal monomial masks has stronger floor from doubled-character norm sqrt(gcd(2,N)N). Exterior perturbation δA,δC yields explicit positive gap; eta.01 limit floor≈.639505 and necessary phase-rank fraction≈.993199. One complex cyclic Green can nevertheless have phase rankN in linear work.','Positive entrywise middle; controlled exterior factors; nonzero entries and invertibility guards.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_phase36/REVIEW.md'],'Quantitative phase-coherence refinement of classical Sinkhorn calibration; high phase rank not computational difficulty.','Arbitrary complex middle or large exterior changes evade theorem; exact algebraic scaling not supplied by approximate iterations.','Accepted scoped gate, subordinate F058.',sources=('gauss',))
add('M-SEED-BALANCE','Balanced Fourier seed and weak-coupling obstruction','A bi-regular right factor forces a precise leverage condition on the left factor.','For F=A D B with B invertible bi-regular, A[0,i](A^−1)[i,0]=1/N for all i is necessary and, with an unrestricted B, sufficient. If A=c(I+E),||E||2<1/2, impossible N≥2. Positive scalar sums of permutation resolvents with all coupling magnitudes<1/3 fall under this obstruction.','One internal monomial, bi-regular right factor; stated scalar coupling/positive combination restrictions.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_phase35/REVIEW.md'],'Clean normalization and weak-coupling veto; finite N8/N16 polynomial exclusions are scoped companions.','The sufficient B can hide Fourier; arbitrary endpoint masks not covered; first-cross calibration verifies2N−1 entries only.','Supporting gate, unranked.',sources=('girs',))
add('M-N64-LIFT','N16-to-N64 lift and sector obstructions','One exact small solution does not extend by copying its inner layers.','Fixed routed N64 eight-Green outer layer cannot complete copied N16 inner layers, by exact9×9 augmented minor enclosure. Every commuting or anticommuting one-inner prefix is excluded. Any successful unrestricted one-inner lift must have each cross-sector block rank≥4, odd component rank≥8, and at least4 unequal coefficient pairs; no diagonal-sector invertibility assumption needed.','Fixed eight cycles, poles1/2...1/9, row-only masks and prescribed F8 bank.',[M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_n64_outer_gate/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0038_construction_and_source_synthesis/reviews/review_one_inner_sector/INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.md'],'Exact finite continuation failure and strengthened mixing requirement tied to certified algebraic N16 root.','Unrestricted one-inner and full1536-variable system open. Mixing rank is not cost.','Finite negative gate, unranked.',sources=('alpha','nullity'),related=('C09',))
add('M-N3-POSITIVE','Exact three-point two-Green chirp control','The smallest odd forced-feedback matrix does have a guarded two-Green representation.','At N3, B=(A+F^−1)^−1 admits κD[(I−tP)^−1+(I−tP^−1)^−1]D, where t²+t=2e/d in a quadratic extension of Q(ω). Both roots satisfy t≠0 and1−t³≠0.','Fixed three-dimensional complex target and supplied algebraic quadratic root.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_n3_positive/REVIEW.md'],'Small exact positive control for same feedback family, not an infinite construction.','No asymptotic extension or finite-field-to-complex existence inference.','Finite control, unranked.',sources=('green',),related=('C01','M-CHIRP-CUBIC'))
add('M-CHIRP-NECESSARY','Forced chirp inverse-support and nonlinear N13 gates','The forced chirp target resists several simple Green representations for independent reasons.','For odd N and legal chirp denominator, B^−1 has a full row, so a product of L monomial-ended cyclic Greens needs2^L≥N. Complementary cut ranks equal Fourier inverse cut ranks; natural half-cut rankfloor(N/2), forcing mean circular displacement≥(N−1)/(2r) for r diagonal-ended occurrences. Specific noncommuting N13 orders have a division-free4×4 coefficient determinant60131 mod65521≠0, excluding every weight and singular endpoint mask in those fixed orders.','Primitive-root fields with char not dividing2N and legal1+NG; N13 lift complex, fixed cycle pair.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_chirp_resolvent_gates/REVIEW.md',M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_chirp_two_green_minor/REVIEW.md'],'Coefficient gate can reject a fixed pair passing all half-cut capacities; necessary structural tools classical.','No arbitrary paired-Green impossibility; finite-field diagonal density can fail; cuts require charged routing; no DAG runtime conclusion.','Subordinate feedback exclusions.',sources=('nullity','girs'),related=('C01','M-CHIRP-LOWER'))
add('M-SPARSE-BRIDGE','Two additive Green sums sparse bridge','Two sums can be rewritten as a sparse-denominator coefficient identity with exact guards.','For invertible A,B,C,D and M=(A^−1+B^−1)(C^−1+D^−1), A M D=(A+B)(CB)^−1(C+D). M=F iff det(CB) AFD=(A+B)adj(CB)(C+D). Literal I−weighted-cycle denominators give3-sparse sums and4-sparse CB; general independent monomial gauges raise sum bound to4.','Exact algebraic equivalence, individually invertible denominators.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_two_sum_bridge/BRIDGE_AUDIT.md'],'Useful denominator-cleared reformulation; elementary inverse/adjugate algebra, not new synthesis.','Determinant condition alone insufficient; singular guards indispensable; supplied CB inverse is two cheap solves. No factor existence or exclusion.','Known mechanism/tool, unranked.',sources=('girs',))
add('M-SPARSE-PREFIX','Sparse-preconditioned full-spark separation','Prime Fourier additive separation bounds survive a row-sparse inverse preconditioner.','For all-square-minors-nonsingular T=P^−1 ΣH_j, P invertible row-s-sparse, d independent ordering pairs, R=sumr_j, floor(N/(s2^d))≤R. Hence prime Fourier with t single Green prefixes plus Q additive tails requires p<(Q+1)2^(t+Q). t1,Q2 fails prime≥29; t2,Q2 fails prime≥53.','Complex full-spark targets; fixed all-input factorization; transposed column-sparse suffix version.',[M+'additions/0037_exact_seed_and_gates/review_two_sum_bridge/source_text/THEOREM.md'],'Asymmetric simultaneous separation plus classical full-spark mixing extends additive theorem through sparse preconditioning.','No composite Fourier full-spark assumption; no two-additive-sum product coverage; approximate gap depends on fixed preconditioner conditioning. Source proof inspected, earlier separate audit exists in lineage.','Supporting distinct restricted theorem, unranked pending targeted priority comparison.',status='source proof inspected; historical scoped audit cited, not freshly replayed',sources=('tao','girs'),related=('M-SEPARATION','M-SPARSE-BRIDGE'))
add('M-TWISTED-DISPLACEMENT','Twisted-displacement logarithmic stage obstruction','A controlled phase alphabet cannot synthesize Fourier through too few affine-conjugated path-resolvent stages.','For t product stages with b=Πq_j expanded branches,d distinct phases and branch displacementrν, exact Fourier implies N≤d(1+Σrν)≤b+ρt b²,ρ2 common path or4 independent affine conjugation. Constant branch count per stage forces logarithmic t.','Constant-coefficient tridiagonal path inverses; affine conjugations and diagonal powers D^a only.',[M+'additions/1717/twisted_bound_review/REVIEW.md'],'Twisted polynomial annihilator applied to cyclic Weyl spectrum; restricted displacement method.','Arbitrary diagonal masks, independent left/right affine maps and free bare affine multipliers excluded. No unrestricted complexity lower bound.','Accepted supporting grammar theorem.',sources=('girs','gauss'))
add('M-PERMUTATION-DISPLACEMENT','Sharp all-permutation Fourier displacement minimum','No input permutation makes one-cycle Fourier displacement low rank.','For primitive-root Fourier, rank(ZF−FP)=N−z(P), where z counts permutation cycles with index sum0 modN. Minimum over all P isfloor(N/2), uniquely negation.','One fixed cyclic output shift and one input permutation; exact displacement rank.',[M+'additions/2156_2159/review_green/extracted/fft_permutation_displacement_gate_v16(1)/fft_permutation_displacement_gate_v16/RESEARCH.md'],'Sharp elementary cycle decomposition, specialized restricted recurrence obstruction.','Source proof read; no standalone current independent review located. Correction-space dimension not arithmetic complexity; adaptive transcript subclaims separately algorithmic.','Supporting theorem, unranked.',status='source proof inspected; independent audit not located',sources=('girs',))
add('M-SCAN-DIMENSION','Multistage scan dimension and finite gauge completeness','Generic matrix coverage grows by a precisely bounded number of parameters per scan stage.','For separated-generator QS1 chart and t stages with fixed permutations, image dimension≤min(N²,N+t(4N−6)). Exact equality certified at N8,16,32 repeatedbitrev through t=N/4+1. Immediately below saturation tangent nullspaces at saved points consist exactly of local and interstage diagonal gauges, dimensions20,72,272.','Complex Zariski closure, separated-generator chart, generic matrices rather than fixed Fourier.',[M+'additions/0536_final_static_review_closure/packages/nested_macro_source_review_0447/evidence/e498e7b16cbaac2ded9976f8ef0222aa990c750b6fd18a73cf3b47ba650885f7__PROOF_CERTIFICATE.md'],'Classical fiber-dimension mechanism plus exact finite Jacobian certificates.','Generic exclusion cannot exclude Fourier; not every singular QS1 chart; finite equality/gauge completeness not allN. Source certificates not executed this pass.','Supporting finite algebraic geometry, unranked.',status='source proof inspected; saved exact certificate assertions not replayed',sources=('alpha',))
add('M-SORTING-RANK','Stable-sort correction rank and all-stride probability','Random binary sorting usually destroys low-rank correction to every cyclic reference stride.','Rank(W−Z^a)=N−cycles(Z^−a W). Stable binary sort with T internal transitions gives rank(W−Z)=2floor(T/2), distribution Pr(r2k)=2^(1−N)binom(N,2k+1), meanN/2−1,varN/4 forN≥3. Explicit union bound gives allstrides rank≥N/8 with probability→1.','IID fair binary words; exact sorted cyclic successor and original cyclic powers.',[M+'additions/1845/rank_audit/RANK_AUDIT.md'],'Exact distribution and uniform-over-strides correction to fixed-reference heuristic.','Mixed two-run words T1 have zero defect; everystride computation is O(N²), notO(N); high rank can remain easy to apply.','Accepted restricted probabilistic result, unranked.',sources=('girs',))
add('M-CRT-TRANSFER','Complementary CRT transfer rank and unique sparsest split','Every balanced root split has full transfer rank, and the sparsest literal split is the usual even/odd FFT.','For balanced partition of N2m distinct Fourier roots, remainder maps R_A,R_B have invertible difference. Combined literal support≥2m, equality iff root polynomialsz^m±1, hence parity split up to exchange. Exact N16 rootpolynomial histogram and modular transfer histograms accepted.','Monomial quotient bases, distinct roots, literal transfer support.',[M+'additions/2351_constructive_gates/review_hero17_phase8/PHASE8_AUDIT.md'],'Exact uniqueness statement in a classical CRT/Fiduccia interface.','Modular nonperiodic support94 gives complex lower bound, not equality. Optional invertible-baseline sharpness falseN2/GF3; main CRT theorem unaffected. Literal support not circuit cost.','Known-framework specialized refinement, unranked.',sources=('delvaux','ailon'))
add('M-GLOBAL-STAGES','Linear-work global stages escaping simple rank gates','High rank, good conditioning and global mixing can coexist with linear-time application.','Corpus gives parity-reordered two-path Green sums, random two-path SPD sums withκ2≤5, square-grid two-path sums, and unitary Cayley/involution constructions. These are explicit stage primitives with O(N) arithmetic and charged routing; saved theorems assert order-robust growing balanced-cut ranks and quantitative singular-value bounds in their separate models.','Single constructed stage, not Fourier factorization; randomness/exact field and pivot hypotheses as specified.',[M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/baseline_queue1_rows100_139/source_texts/123_c2910b74adec2a84.md',M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/baseline_queue1_rows60_79/source_texts/70_bb50b47b4dd8e085.md',M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/baseline_queue1_rows60_79/source_texts/75_c61066edce57927b.md',M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/baseline_queue1_rows40_59/source_texts/40_bbcae332d0a0f510.md',M+'additions/0216_review_completion_and_extensions/baseline_queue2_main136/source_texts/083_86f6a5c8be17e1e7.inert.txt'],'Standard Green/Cayley/expander mechanisms provide counterexamples to overbroad rank-as-cost intuition.','This pass inspected construction/status excerpts, not every all-order probability/singular-value proof. Exact constants and latest theorem-level audit require further reconciliation before ranking. No Fourier synthesis claimed.','Retained distinct construction family; unranked needs deeper review.',status='construction excerpts inspected; quantitative theorem audits need reconciliation',category='needs review',sources=('girs','expander'))
add('M-WINDOW-GRAM','Fourier interval-window, tail and real-Gram gates','Several exact row/column compatibility tests constrain two-stage models.','Three-sided interval-window lemma yields sharpened N≤9r²+7r for four oriented QS budgets≤r, natural/affine input order and arbitrary output order. Forr1 filter largest feasibleN16, not factorization. Tail inequalities min(t,ℓ)≤rC_down+rB_up and mirror hold. For fixed real invertible A, F=A Q P B with complex diagonalQ and real invertibleB iff every column of A is reflection-even/odd; connected Gram support veto is only necessary.','Specified two-stage orientations and Fourier endpoint order; real-factor one-mask theorem separate.',[M+'additions/1825/window_audit/WINDOW_AUDIT.md',M+'additions/1807/bilateral_audit/BILATERAL_TAIL_GATE_AUDIT.md',M+'additions/1807/phase22_audit/PHASE22_AUDIT.md'],'Sharper necessary filter and exact one-mask classification, mostly elementary rank/real-imaginary decomposition.','Window bound superseded by stronger cutoffs in narrower families; filter sharpness is not existence. Other Gram/real-resolvent evaluator subclaims algorithmic.','Historical supporting tools, unranked.',sources=('girs','gauss'),related=('M-TWO-STAGE',))
add('M-FIXED-POLE-N4','Complete projective fixed-pole N4 exclusion','A specific three-mixer model fails even after all finite and infinite coupling charts are included.','For G0=(I−Z/4)^−1,G1=(I−V/5)^−1,V cycle(0,2,1,3), no F4=H_a L H_b M H_c with H_[u:v]=uG0+vG1, all three projective pairs nonzero and masks invertible. Covers zero-entry middle support and all projective infinities.','Fixed poles/cycles and identity internal permutations; complex masks.',[M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_nonaffine_green_parameters/full_fixed_pole_checkpoint/FULL_FIXED_POLE_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2213_ongoing/review_nonaffine_green_parameters/equal_outer_checkpoint/EQUAL_OUTER_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2213_ongoing/review_nonaffine_green_parameters/one_infinite_checkpoint/ONE_INFINITE_OUTER_REVIEW.md'],'Completed exceptional-stratum elimination for narrow finite pencil.','Variable-pole positiveN4 unaffected; not allGreen exclusion. Earlier equal-outer and one-infinite rows subordinate to complete result.','Finite negative certificate, unranked.',sources=('alpha',))
add('M-PARTIAL-COLUMNS','Exact partial-column Green interpolation and projective windows','Fitting a few Fourier columns is possible and does not imply a complete transform.','For q fixed Hamiltonian Green responses and q selected target columns with all entries nonzero, generic legal scalar couplings yield unique all-nonzero row gauges matching those columns. Matchingq+1 generically impossible. Deterministic dominating-power choice proves existence with huge exponents; q=N gives quadratic online work. Separate five-generator 3×4 projective-window Macaulay35×35 certificates exclude all mappingsN4,N8; N16 evidence sampled only.','One-sided row masks, fixed generator cycles; finite projective window mappings.',[M+'additions/2333_source_reviews/review_green_new_2307/checkpoint/SEPARATION_AND_PHASE32_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_green_new_2257/checkpoint/NEW_GREEN_ARCHIVE_REVIEW.md'],'Useful precise interpolation/completion boundary and finite Macaulay exclusion.','No arbitrary input-side gauges or products; N1 sampling law needs separate guard; passing selected-column tests not full Fourier equality.','Supporting constructive/certificate family, unranked.',sources=('alpha',))
add('M-LOCAL-ANNIHILATOR','Local annihilator and three-stage layout witnesses','Small supported vectors expose local Fourier mismatch in restricted scan layouts.','Interior windowW has annihilator dimension≥W−2r. Casoratian of s independent widthw polynomials has degree≤s(w−s) after removing z^(s(s−1)/2) and is nonzero. Boundary-aware construction gives explicit rank-one two-stage witness forN≥18. Three-stage equality requires rankT[I,J]≤2r1+2r3+r2+k(layout), with endpoint improvements.','Natural/affine Fourier endpoints; exact primitive-root field; QS cuts include degenerate generators.',[M+'additions/2115/multistage/research/MULTISTAGE_PHASE28_AUDIT.md'],'Explicit local witness rather than existential rank certificate; classical Vandermonde/Cauchy–Binet base.','Does not improve stronger existentialN17 cutoff; nonaffine endpoints require actual blockrank. Internal-phase finite exclusions remain fixed generator families.','Supporting witness/tool, unranked.',sources=('girs','tao'),related=('C04','M-TWO-STAGE'))
add('M-N4-GAUGE-RECURSION','Finite N4 synthesis and exact gauge-closed stage recursion','A variable-pole finite solution and a closed stage identity are real but do not supply a dyadic Fourier recursion.','Certified algebraicN4 product of3 two-cycle Green sums withvariable poles and two diagonal masks has all6 denominators and all mixer entries nonzero. Gauged family A_N(p,q,t,d) has exact contiguous-half block recursion, with separatep0 boundary. Natural-term off-block correction compresses to a k×k cyclic factor tensor rank1 and has exact exceptional-locus rank formula.','Specific dyadic natural/bitrev cycles; stage identities versus Fourier synthesis kept separate.',[M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_nonaffine_green_parameters/variable_poles_checkpoint/VARIABLE_POLES_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_nonaffine_green_parameters/gauge_recursion_checkpoint/GAUGE_RECURSION_REVIEW.md',M+'additions/2318_reviewed/review_nonaffine_green_parameters/accumulated_correction_checkpoint/ACCUMULATED_CORRECTION_REVIEW.md'],'Finite certified positive plus exact family closure; no allsize coefficient recurrence.','Correction compression is for natural term, notwholetwo-termstage; wholeproduct rank onlyupperbound. Complete rankformula retained in evidence, not rederived inthispass.','Finite control and supporting identities, unranked.',sources=('alpha','girs'),related=('M-FIXED-POLE-N4',))
add('M-F8-LOCAL-ELIMINATION','F8 inverse-chart, jet, dual/onion and spectral gates','Exact elimination reduces one small feasibility problem without solving its missing branches.','FixedpermutationF8 separated-generator two-stage model has regularpatch30 equations26 coordinates; onepoint secondorder nonliftability by61×61 determinant6913mod12289. Dual/onion reductions give20 equations16coords then12 rational equations8coords with29guards. Spectral adjacent-tail relations partly avoid old divisions. GF17 openchart exhausts1,328,244 gamma pairs,2546invertiblecandidates,zero fullsecondstage successes.','Localized normalized charts with invertibility/corner/denominator guards; fixedpermutation[7,0,6,3,4,1,2,5].',[M+'additions/1450/algebraic/ALGEBRAIC_JET_INDEPENDENT_AUDIT.md',M+'additions/1628/audits/dual_onion/INDEPENDENT_DUAL_AUDIT.md',M+'additions/1646/SPECTRAL_DETERMINANT_AUDIT.md',M+'additions/1646/finite_field_audit/INDEPENDENT_GF17_AUDIT.md'],'Exact smaller compatibility descriptions and finite local obstruction; algebraic elimination mechanisms classical.','Finitefield point emptiness does not implycomplex/geometricemptiness. Different diag(A)/diag(A^-1) charts differ; excludedbranches remain; finiteF8 fullfeasibility unresolved.','Historical supporting elimination chain, unranked.',sources=('alpha',),related=('M-NONLINEAR-COMPATIBILITY',))
