add('M-MULTISCALE-CHIRP','Multiscale Weyl-support and dyadic chirp product barrier','A dyadic chirp needs more than the support-count minimum number of pure-shift resolvents.','For N2^m≥4 and primitive2Nthrootζ, Cij=ζ^((i−j)^2) has inversecoeffq_t=ζ^(−t²)/N. Any literal product of pure-shift resolvents with arbitrary strides and Weylmonomial gauges needsL≥m+1: equalitym in supportcount forces unique dyadic subset sums, contradicted by chirp parallelogram ratio. Moregenerally inverseWeylsupport ofFourierN²odd,N²/2even impliesΠq_j≥thatnumber forq_j-atomdenominators. Binaryreshaperankq=2^min(a,m−a).','Literal multiplicative Weyl/shift grammar, specified roots, noarbitrarydiagonalgauges.',[D+'fft_hero17_phase15_multiscale_weyl_chirp_2026-10-10/PROOF_CERTIFICATE.md'],'Candidate one-step sharpening beyond classical support-product count; dyadic chirp equality-case argument could merit focused audit. Fourier Weyl Gauss support and geometric fusion classical.','No matchingm+1construction; noadditivesum/DAGbound. Classical multiscale product fuses to oneO(N)Green, provingfactorcountnotruntime. Missing independent checkofallfield/stridedegeneracy and prioritycomparison.','Interesting source-level restricted sharpening; unranked pending independent review.',status='source theorem analytically inspected; independent audit pending',sources=('gauss',),related=('M-MAGNETIC-SPAN','M-WEYL-BRANCH'),inspection=newinspect)
