by['M-MULTISCALE-CHIRP'].update(exact_claim='For N=2^m≥4 and a primitive 2N-th root ζ, C[i,j]=ζ^((i−j)^2) has inverse coefficients q_t=ζ^(−t²)/N. Every literal product of pure-shift resolvents with arbitrary strides and Weyl-monomial gauges representing C needs L≥m+1. Equality L=m in the support count would force unique dyadic subset sums, contradicted by a chirp parallelogram ratio. More generally, Fourier inverse Weyl support is N² for odd N and N²/2 for even N, so products of denominators having q_j Weyl atoms need Πq_j at least that support. The binary reshape of q has rank 2^min(a,m−a).', model='Literal multiplicative Weyl/shift grammar with specified roots; arbitrary diagonal gauges excluded.', novelty_delta='Candidate one-step sharpening beyond the classical support-product count. The dyadic chirp equality-case argument merits focused audit. Fourier/Gauss support and geometric resolvent fusion are classical.', limitations='No matching m+1 construction, additive-sum bound, or shared-DAG bound. A classical multiscale product fuses into one O(N) Green solve, so factor count is not runtime. Independent checking of field and stride degeneracies, plus focused priority comparison, remain open.')
by['M-TWO-SIDED-GAUGE'].update(exact_claim='For even s≥4, N=s², and the half-y-grid shift Π, a Π-commuting T0 cannot satisfy F=D_out T0 D_in^−1 with arbitrary invertible diagonal endpoints. For unitary endpoint gauges, both operator and relative Frobenius distance are at least g_s=(1/2)sqrt(1−ρ), where ρ=2/[s sin(π/s)]; the limit is about 0.3014051. After k occurrence-wise weight edits the uniform gap is at least (1/2)sqrt(max(0,1−ρ−8k/N)), so exact equality requires k≥ceil(N(1−ρ)/8). Generic gauges give the stronger k≥N/2, but that is not uniform over gauges.', model='Fixed grid involution and legal commuting reference. Exact arbitrary-invertible-gauge impossibility is distinct from the metric result for unitary gauges.', novelty_delta='A substantive two-sided extension of the Phase16 common-gauge theorem, with an explicit rank-four phase-matrix spectrum and uniform edit floor. Paired monomial normalization and orthogonal projection are classical ingredients.', limitations='The s=2 exception is retained. The gap is not claimed sharp across all gauges. No uniform metric bound is established for arbitrary nonunitary endpoints. The new section-nine edit bound still needs an independent audit.')
by['M-OUTER-STABILITY'].update(exact_claim='For one fixed four-QS1-stage N=256 layout, the transformed middle H=P3^−1 C4 U C1 P1^−1 satisfies 32 parity-block rank requirements below 128. The mask-64 budget is 16. An exact rational fourth-moment lower bound M>1264/25 gives σ17>3sqrt(2)/5. Thus ||C4−D4||·||C1||+||C1−D1||>3sqrt(2)/5 for diagonal unitaries D1,D4. If both deviations are at most ε, then ε>sqrt(1+3sqrt(2)/5)−1, about 0.359606.', model='One specified N256 layout, diagonal-unitary references, and explicitly charged inverse norms in approximation versions.', novelty_delta='A quantitative coefficient restriction after graph-cut capacity tests pass. The narrower fourth-moment part has a historical independent audit; the latest 32-mask packet contains additional source-level claims.', limitations='This is not full infeasibility. Nonunitary diagonal references require their minimum singular values. The expanded latest packet has not been independently replayed.')
by['M-PAIRED-JACOBI'].update(exact_claim='For the fixed N256 layout, paired complementary blocks of a unitary matrix have equal singular values. When both candidate blocks have rank at most 16 and both baseline squared Frobenius norms are 64, the paired squared Frobenius tail and paired nuclear lower bounds are 96. An explicit cell-energy witness attains 96 in the relaxation of all 64 scalar constraints. The denominator-free dual G=P1 S1 U^−1 S4 P3 supplies necessary bilinear outer-stage rank conditions. Conditional on both outer inverses being exactly unitary, the operator gap exceeds sqrt(2−2sqrt(7)/5), about 0.970412, and the common outer perturbation exceeds 0.485206.', model='Classical unitary Jacobi/CS coupling in one fixed layout; the strongest gap requires exactly unitary outer inverses.', novelty_delta='A useful paired-block refinement and polynomial dual interface; Jacobi/CS and best-low-rank tail principles are classical.', limitations='The paired Frobenius bound alone does not improve the single-block operator bound. The energy-relaxation witness is not a factorization. The conditional unitary gap does not apply to arbitrary outer stages. Independent finite-certificate reconstruction remains needed.')
by['M-HADAMARD-SEGRE'].update(exact_claim='For fixed invertible A,B,C with every B entry nonzero, put H=FC^−1. The identity F=L A D B E C with invertible diagonal L,D,E holds iff some vector c has all entries nonzero and Z(c)=(A^−1 diag(c)H) divided entrywise by B has rank one with every entry nonzero. When P0 is invertible, T_j=P0^−1 P_j must have a common eigenvector c with c, P0c and the required eigenvalues all nonzero. A nonzero determinant of [T1,T2] rejects every gauge. Eight source-reported four-/six-Green witnesses at N=3,4,6,8 have guarded nonzero determinants modulo 97 and characteristic-zero nonvanishing lifts.', model='Fixed stage data and ordering, three variable diagonal gauges, and all stated nonzero guards. A singular commutator is only a necessary test.', novelty_delta='The three-gauge Hadamard–Segre formulation and explicit robustness certificate may be project-specific. Diagonal-equivalence methods and common-eigenvector tests are established primary antecedents.', limitations='A singular commutator is not acceptance. The selected witnesses do not exclude every Green weight. Generic failure for fixed wiring is not uniform impossibility. Finite certificates and positive-gap constants still need independent reconstruction.')
by['M-N4-GAUGE-RECURSION']['exact_claim']='A certified algebraic N4 product of three two-cycle Green sums, with variable poles and two diagonal masks, has all six denominators and all mixer entries nonzero. The gauged family A_N(p,q,t,d) has an exact contiguous-half block recursion, with p=0 handled separately. For N=km, the natural-term off-block correction compresses to a k×k cyclic factor tensor a rank-one matrix: for p,d nonzero and p^N≠1 its rank is k−1 when (p^N)^(k−1)=1, and k otherwise; at p=0 its rank is zero. Despite growing rank, the correction has an O(N) application.'
by['M-N4-GAUGE-RECURSION']['limitations']='The correction formula concerns the natural term, not the whole two-term stage. For the complete masked product, telescoping supplies only a rank upper bound. Neither stage closure nor the finite N4 solution supplies an all-size Fourier coefficient recurrence.'
by['M-F8-LOCAL-ELIMINATION']['exact_claim']='For the fixed-permutation F8 separated-generator two-stage model, one regular patch has 30 equations in 26 coordinates. One specified parameter point has a second-order non-liftability certificate from a 61×61 determinant, 6913 modulo 12289. Dual/onion reductions give 20 equations in 16 coordinates and then 12 rational equations in eight coordinates with 29 guards. Spectral adjacent-tail relations avoid some earlier divisions. GF(17) open-chart enumeration examines 1,328,244 gamma pairs and finds 2546 invertible candidates, none satisfying the full second-stage conditions. The four-column compatibility gate factors a selected determinant as −DB·DH; it excludes a specified regular complex slice and bounds the four-variable necessary set dimension by two, with at most twelve exceptional base points.'
